e\":\"cannot tell\",\"bears_on_question\":true,\"why\":\"The proposed Ohio guarantee could add to commitments, but its amount, timing and inclusion in this programme are not stated.\"}\n{\"item\":24,\"change\":\"no\",\"bears_on_question\":true,\"why\":\"Slower AI-agent progress could affect demand, but does not quantify its effect on 2027 spending.\"}\n{\"item\":25,\"change\":\"no\",\"bears_on_question\":true,\"why\":\"Google Cloud growth suggests demand, but does not quantify a change to the four companies’ 2026 data-center spending.\"}\n{\"item\":26,\"change\":\"no\",\"bears_on_question\":true,\"why\":\"The announced credit-support model is already reflected as directional support for the Ohio forecast.\"}\n{\"item\":27,\"change\":\"no\",\"bears_on_question\":true,\"why\":\"Higher NVIDIA shipment expectations suggest demand, but do not quantify the four companies’ 2026 data-center spending.\"}\n{\"item\":28,\"change\":\"no\",\"bears_on_question\":true,\"why\":\"The capacity-repurchase arrangement describes a support mechanism, but does not establish an Ohio lease guarantee.\"}\n{\"item\":29,\"change\":\"no\",\"bears_on_question\":true,\"why\":\"Sharon’s backstop is a precedent already reflected in the reasons, not an Ohio guarantee.\"}\n{\"item\":30,\"change\":\"no\",\"bears_on_question\":true,\"why\":\"Lease backstopping supports the existing forecast, but the passage does not identify an Ohio agreement.\"}\n{\"item\":31,\"change\":\"no\",\"bears_on_question\":false,\"why\":\"The revenue and margin forecast does not address authorization for the three firms to buy H200 chips.\"}\n{\"item\":32,\"change\":\"no\",\"bears_on_question\":true,\"why\":\"Slower AI-agent progress could affect demand, but does not quantify its effect on 2026 spending.\"}\n{\"item\":33,\"change\":\"no\",\"bears_on_question\":true,\"why\":\"The statement is a counterweight, but it does not specifically address permission for the three firms or the deadline.\"}\n{\"item\":34,\"change\":\"no\",\"bears_on_question\":true,\"why\":\"Firmus customer revenue is not NVIDIA’s credit-support commitment and does not establish a different commitment amount.\"}\n{\"item\":35,\"change\":\"no\",\"bears_on_question\":true,\"why\":\"A rejected backup design reinforces execution difficulties, but does not point to a launch before the deadline.\"}\n{\"item\":36,\"change\":\"no\",\"bears_on_question\":true,\"why\":\"Higher NVIDIA shipment expectations suggest demand, but do not quantify the four companies’ 2026 data-center spending.\"}\n{\"item\":37,\"change\":\"no\",\"bears_on_question\":true,\"why\":\"The hyperscaler spending forecast provides general demand context, but does not establish whether NVIDIA will sign the Ohio guarantee.\"}"}}
